in indonesia's south kalimantan province  on the island of borneo  heavy rain has lashed these villages and  towns for days  tens of thousands of people have been  evacuated  some are choosing to stay put fawzi  rahman has been sleeping outside his  house for nearly a week  it's the first time he's experienced a  flood  i have to stay here to look after my  belongings people might steal them at  night  also i have to watch in case the  electricity short circuits  flooding is common in indonesia during  the monsoon season  but this year 11 of the 13 districts in  south kalimantan have been inundated  some for the first time ever bantuaname  i need help the basics like food we  cannot work right now and my husband  hasn't been able to work because of  covet 19.  evacuation centers are operating around  affected areas  but volunteers say their resources are  stretched  we need blankets for the elderly we only  have three we need food for them  and for the toddlers we're also lacking  medicine  some of those here are suffering from  diarrhea and skin infections caused by  contaminated water  and many say they don't know what  they'll do when they return to their  houses  all my possessions are gone the water in  my house is chest height  president joko widodo visited the area  earlier in the week  this is a major flood that may not have  occurred in south carolina for more than  50 years due to heavy rainfall  but environmental groups say land  degradation and  deforestation is making the floods worse  these floods are particularly bad  because from the total 3.7 million  hectares of land in south carolina  50 is already burdened by mining and  palm oil plantations  for him and others this crisis isn't  just about  rain but the mismanagement of land  jessica washington  al jazeera jakarta
 

